@Caleigh Runge-Hottman FYI, I pinged ppisar who is an SME on modularity asking if there is way for developers how to force re-building all the module RPMs when they build a new module and he told me that there is this option they can use:
rhpkg module-build --optional rebuild_strategy=all
This is an another potential work-around here = developers re-building all module RPMs when building a new module version to ensure they all can be safely PQC signed.

